I have implemented the `UserProfile` component as an async server component, following the pattern found in `app/page.tsx`. This component fetches data from `/api/users/profile` and includes a fallback to mock data in case the fetch fails (mirroring the error handling strategy in the existing `getProducts` function).

Here is the implementation:

```typescript:app/UserProfile.tsx
interface User {
  name: string;
  email: string;
}

async function getUserProfile() {
  try {
    const res = await fetch('/api/users/profile');
    return res.json();
  } catch (error) {
    return {
      name: 'John Doe',
      email: 'john@example.com',
    };
  }
}

export default async function UserProfile() {
  const user = await getUserProfile();

  return (
    <div>
      <h2>User Profile</h2>
      <div>Name: {user.name}</div>
      <div>Email: {user.email}</div>
    </div>
  );
}
```
